nd the walk escapes\n      source_undefined -> None. Unearned refutation impossible; recall is lost instead,\n      which is the safe direction.\n\nSo both shapes I could construct are already safe, by two different mechanisms. That is\nNOT a proof that no third shape exists, and the difference between those two statements\nis exactly what this item is for.\n\nHOW TO SETTLE IT, and it is a sweep rather than a guess -- guessing shapes is what nearly\ngot L4 recorded as unreal (one Go func-literal candidate failed before a mechanical sweep\nfound three real ones in twenty minutes). Instrument: walk the production path over a\ncorpus, and for every walk that returns False, re-derive the function's true def/use with\na second, independent reading (the extractor's own conservative _collect_identifiers is\none candidate; a second is the leaf enumeration without the defines restriction) and\nreport every disagreement. A False that survives both readings is earned; one that does\nnot names the third shape.\n\nDO NOT RE-OPEN INV-lupav ON THIS WITHOUT A REPRODUCED CASE. The invariant closed on its\nfiled row with an enumeration (five accounted-for exits, pinned structurally by\ntest_walk_exit_census.py) and fifteen swept cases with controls. This is the disclosed\nedge of that enumeration, filed per the standing ruling CLOSE ON THE FILED ROW, FILE THE\nRESIDUAL."  # 6553
